course: dictionary
lesson: 11992
title: Chanted: words said together
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Chanted is the past form of chant. When you chant, you say or sing the same words again and again in a rhythm, often loudly and together with other people. «The fans chanted his name all through the match.» The fans did not sing one long song. They repeated his name over and over, all together.
explain: Chanted can also mean sung on one or a few notes, as monks chant prayers in church. «The monks chanted their prayers at dawn.» Here chanted is about singing slowly on just a few notes, not about shouting.
explain: Look at the clues around the word. Crowds, rhymes, slogans and times tables all tell you that the words were repeated together. Use the swap test: «The fans said his name all through the match» still makes sense, so chanted means said or sung again and again together.
fact: Chant means to say or sing the same words again and again in a rhythm.
fact: Chanted is the past form of chant, so it tells you about something that already happened.
fact: «Chanted» can describe a crowd at a football match or a protest, or children saying a rhyme in the playground.
fact: In church, monks and nuns chant prayers on a few notes, and many faiths use chanting in worship.
fact: Chanted can also be a verb for saying times tables together in class: «The class chanted the times tables.»
exercise: «The protesters chanted slogans outside the town hall.» What did the protesters do? | Ran away from the town hall | Sat quietly and read books | Drew pictures of the town hall | *Said the same slogans again and again together
exercise: «The class chanted the seven times table before the test.» What does chanted mean here? | Whispered one number to the teacher | *Said the words together in a steady rhythm | Forgot the words quickly | Wrote the numbers in neat rows
exercise: Which word is the past form of chant? | *chanted | chants | chant | chanting
test: «The crowd chanted his name, again and again.» What does chanted mean? | Argued about the score | *Said or sang the same words together, again and again | Walked slowly away | Ate their lunch quickly
test: In RE, the monks chanted psalms on a few notes. What does chanted suggest? | Danced in a circle around the church | Drew pictures of the church windows | Shouted angrily at each other | *Sang slowly on just a few notes
exam: Which sentence uses chanted correctly? | *The girl chanted a skipping rhyme with her friends at break | The girl chanted the playground door shut | The girl chanted her lunch box quickly | The girl chanted a sandwich for lunch
